{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["And he said to one of them: 'Your servant' — for he magnified him in his own eyes. Also among the angels are officers. And the tav of מות is elided in the tav of וָמַתִּי, for tav and yod are a sign of the hif'il in verbs, and this was so because two tavs are joined. Likewise תַּשְׁחִית and וְכָרָתָ (Deuteronomy 20:20)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "Reading היjיד as הי\"ד, an abbreviation for הפעיל or היפעל (hif'il); the lone j confirms a corrupted or non-standard abbreviation. The elision explanation parallels the crasis in וָמַתִּי (from וּמוֹת + י)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:11.633187209Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}